content:
Help me find the associations.  

#### Data:
These are the extracted domain objects and their associations:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "description": "Person placing orders and receiving deliveries."
    },
    {
      "name": "Restaurant",
      "description": "Food provider offering meals to customers."
    },
    {
      "name": "Food Order",
      "description": "Order placed by a customer for a meal.",
      "attributes": [
        "Restaurant",
        "Meal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Meal",
      "description": "Prepared food item included in a food order."
    },
    {
      "name": "Meal Package",
      "description": "Packaged meal prepared for pickup.",
      "attributes": [
        "Food Order"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Pick Up",
      "description": "Event where a driver collects the meal package."
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery Driver",
      "description": "Driver responsible for picking up and delivering orders."
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery",
      "description": "Process of transporting a meal package to a customer.",
      "attributes": [
        "Delivery Status",
        "Meal Package"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery Status",
      "description": "State of the delivery"
    },
    {
      "name": "Support Agent",
      "description": "Staff member resolving customer issues."
    },
    {
      "name": "Issue Report",
      "description": "Customer-submitted problem related to an order."
    },
    {
      "name": "Refund",
      "description": "Compensation issued to a customer for a valid issue."
    },
    {
      "name": "Restaurant Staff Member",
      "description": "Staff preparing and packaging food orders."
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Task:
- Draw connections between objects that have an association. 
- Name each object and add a description that captures the meaning of the association.
- Return the associations in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "associations": [
    {
      "from": "...",
      "to": "...",
      "description": "..."
    }
  ]
}
```

Here are the associations:
```json
{
  "associations": [
    {
      "from": "Customer",
      "to": "Restaurant",
      "description": "Customer browses available restaurants."
    },
    {
      "from": "Customer",
      "to": "Food Order",
      "description": "Customer places a food order."
    },
    {
      "from": "Restaurant Staff Member",
      "to": "Food Order",
      "description": "Restaurant Staff Member accepts the food order."
    },
    {
      "from": "Restaurant Staff Member",
      "to": "Meal Package",
      "description": "Restaurant Staff Member packages the meal."
    },
    {
      "from": "Delivery Driver",
      "to": "Pick Up",
      "description": "Delivery Driver performs the pickup."
    },
    {
      "from": "Pick Up",
      "to": "Meal Package",
      "description": "Pick Up handles the meal package."
    },
    {
      "from": "Delivery Driver",
      "to": "Delivery",
      "description": "Delivery Driver carries out the delivery."
    },
    {
      "from": "Delivery",
      "to": "Customer",
      "description": "Delivery reaches the customer."
    },
    {
      "from": "Customer",
      "to": "Issue Report",
      "description": "Customer submits an issue report."
    },
    {
      "from": "Support Agent",
      "to": "Issue Report",
      "description": "Support Agent reviews the issue report."
    },
    {
      "from": "Support Agent",
      "to": "Refund",
      "description": "Support Agent issues a refund."
    },
    {
      "from": "Refund",
      "to": "Customer",
      "description": "Refund is granted to the customer."
    }
  ]
}
```
